{"availability":"available","full":"tsilva/aigrounds","name":"aigrounds","description":"🧠 Learn AI by experimenting with algorithms 🔬","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-08T17:46:30Z","updated":"2026-10-04T06:51:49Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://aigrounds.tsilva.eu","topics":[],"demo":"https://aigrounds.tsilva.eu/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:23.922Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:23.922Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:23.922Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:49.517Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T06:52:23.922Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["🧠 Learn AI by experimenting with algorithms 🔬","AI Grounds is a web app for people learning artificial intelligence through hands-on experiments. Move data points, tune parameters, and step through algorithms to see how their behavior changes. Try the live playgrounds to explore statistics, probability, neural networks, and more.","The gallery follows a learning sequence and distinguishes published lessons from planned ones. Many lessons guide you through Predict → Try → Explain, with an optional AI Guide to talk through the result. Probability lessons connect exact outcome counts, model expectations and reference groups to the formulas through guided experiments. Use a desktop or laptop: screens below 768 pixels show a notice instead of the playgrounds."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tsilva/aigrounds/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d07c180af9b1e8cae4a3140f48658a34ac1fb5011a49a023a6c014c774fc5ff9","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:24.002Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:24.002Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"🧠 Learn AI by experimenting with algorithms 🔬","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tsilva/aigrounds/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d07c180af9b1